### Review feedback on the previously reviewed head (`075c58ff61b`)

- **P2, "Exclude stopped services from the running-build comparison"** — fixed in `65eabfc22e0`: the gatherer now requires the registered service to be loaded **and** `runtime.status === "running"` **and**, when its PID is known and the port has listeners, to own one of them, before the service's `packageBuildId` is offered for comparison. `228f8a091a8` pins the listener-ownership half beside the existing target-selection regression, and `65eabfc22e0` adds the unloaded-service negative case. Both land under the real-behavior case 3 above.

### Regression tests

17 cases across `src/gateway/stale-install.test.ts`, `src/daemon/service-layout.test.ts`, `src/cli/daemon-cli/status.print.test.ts` and `src/cli/daemon-cli/status.gather.test.ts` (via `status.gather.service-inspection.test-support.ts`) cover: export mismatch attributed only after a replacement is recorded with both builds named; a missing chunk annotated with the running build when the on-disk identity is unreadable; on-disk build id readable / unwritten / truncated / over-long; one build id and no restart guidance when the install has not moved; both ids plus the restart when `dist` was rebuilt under the running Gateway; a comparison omitted for a Gateway whose install this host cannot read; the registered service's build kept out of a comparison it does not target; **kept out when the service is unloaded**; **kept out when the service's PID does not own the probed port's listener**; and profile / container / default-profile rendering of the restart instruction. The export-mismatch test asserts the negative first — the same `SyntaxError` returns `null` while the installation still matches — so the gate on the recorded replacement is pinned rather than incidental.

### Node error shape for the export-mismatch class

The discriminator the classification depends on, checked directly on Node v24.18.0 rather than assumed:

```
name= SyntaxError
code= undefined
url= undefined
msg= The requested module './lib.mjs' does not provide an export named 'missingThing'
ownProps= ["stack","message"]
```

No `code`, no `url`, no `path`. `isMissingRuntimeChunk` requires `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`/`ENOENT` plus an absolute path inside the install root, so it could never match this class — which is why the live 12:00 failure went unattributed, and why the new classification is gated on an already-recorded installation replacement rather than on the error's shape alone.

