## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: `openclaw path resolve` and `find` return empty values for numeric, boolean, and null Markdown frontmatter values written on an indented continuation line. Inline comments also leak into numeric and empty values.

## User Impact

Frontmatter reads now return `00123`, `false`, and `null` as written, without comment text. This works when another frontmatter entry is malformed, too. Quoted strings, collections, aliases, source lines, and file bytes retain their existing behavior.

## Why This Change Was Made

Use the parsed scalar's source for non-string values, preserving spelling such as leading zeroes, while keeping YAML's decoded value for strings. Apply the same rule to the tolerant reader. Keep inline `---` and `...` values intact when reparsing them would otherwise produce a synthetic null scalar.

## Evidence

- Built the unmodified base and the clean commit with `pnpm build qaRuntime`, then exercised the actual `pnpm --silent openclaw path` entry point on Windows / Node 24.22.1 with an isolated home and only `oc-path` enabled.
- Five new regression cases fail on the base; the final parser suite passes all 38 tests. Two additional marker controls caught and verified the fallback edge case during review.
- Full `oc-path` suite: 489 passed, 5 existing skips, 33 files. Focused production/test typechecks, lint, format, staged test-line ratchet, and `git diff --check` passed.
- Native autoreview: no remaining P0–P3 findings in the complete two-file patch, with unchanged caller and dependency context supplied.
- The captured CLI runs below cover normal and malformed frontmatter, independent `resolve` calls, and an unchanged `set --dry-run` control. All 10 commands exited 0. Both input files remained byte-identical after each run. Full repository tests were not run.

